                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This isn't a low-quality game, and some people might really like it. The only reason I gave it a thumbs down is that like games this old, there was no fast travel map, and the hint only helped if you were in the room where the action could be taken. I've played many games like that that I did like. But the problem here is there is a ton of running around. I don't mind a lot of running around as long as there is a fast travel map and/or good hints. I got to the point where it was just an exercise in frustration.\r\n\r\nThey put effort into this. The mini-games were creative (though some were too tedious for my tastes, but I'll take creative or the same four mini-games you see in a lot of the newer games, even if I skip them).\r\n\r\nI didn't finish the game, so I'm sure it's much longer than 2 hours.",
